{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2127","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Hamed and AghaBalaSar"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Hamid wrote $$$3014$$$ lines of code for the a+b problem and gave $$$10$$$ lines of it to Hamed; then the following problem came to Hamed's mind."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An array $$$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n$$$ is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"snake"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if and only if all of the following conditions hold: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" All elements in $$$a$$$ are integers between $$$0$$$ and $$$m$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_1 + a_2 + \\cdots + a_n = m$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_n=\\max\\left([a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n]\\right)$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We define $$$f(a)$$$ as in the following pseudocode:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"function f(array a):\n    pos := 1\n    res := 0\n    let nxt[x] be an array such that nxt[x] is the smallest index y such that\n                                    y > x and a[y] > a[x],\n                              or undefined if no such y exists\n    while pos < n:\n        if a[pos] < a[n]:\n            res += a[nxt[pos]] - a[pos]\n            pos := nxt[pos]\n        else:\n            pos += 1\n    return res\n"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the sum of $$$f(a)$$$ over all "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"snake"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" arrays $$$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n$$$, modulo $$$10^9+7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$2 \\leq n \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$, $$$0 \\leq m \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the length of a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"snake"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" array and the sum of all elements in a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"snake"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$m$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single integer — the sum of $$$f(a)$$$ over all "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"snake"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" arrays $$$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n$$$, modulo $$$10^9+7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n8\n2 5\n3 4\n4 6\n5 10\n6 23\n100 100\n142857 33333\n200000 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n9\n14\n76\n985\n142112\n771227753\n865580631\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, there are three "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"snake"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" arrays:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$f([0, 5]) = 5$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$f([1, 4]) = 3$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$f([2, 3]) = 1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus, the answer is $$$5+3+1=9$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, there are six "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"snake"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" arrays:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$f([0, 0, 4]) = 4$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$f([0, 1, 3]) = 3$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$f([1, 0, 3]) = 2$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$f([1, 1, 2]) = 1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$f([0, 2, 2]) = 2$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$f([2, 0, 2]) = 2$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus, the answer is $$$4+3+2+1+2+2=14$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fifth test case, a possible "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"snake"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" array is:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$f([3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9]) = 6$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"2127F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2127/problem/F"}